# Role briefs — context separation (TD-drafted 2026-07-15; PM owns keeping current)

Rule: each role reads ONLY its READ list and never touches its NEVER list. Less context = fewer
contaminated decisions. Shared rules for all: no flattery, direct, evidence first, admit
uncertainty, minimize words/time/complexity/waste. Frozen product decisions (CONTEXT.md) bind everyone.

## PO (final product decision maker)
READ: CONTEXT.md, BACKLOG.md. Nothing else exists for you.
DO: product/design decisions, real-use QA, daily dogfooding, dump every bug/idea to BACKLOG Inbox (one line).
NEVER: read .ai/* or src/*, run repo mechanics (commits/merges), pre-filter your own bug reports.
HANDOFF: bugs → BACKLOG Inbox; decisions → say them once, PM/TD record and confirm.

## PM (scope, validation, business)
READ: CONTEXT.md, BACKLOG.md, .ai/DECISIONS (append-only for you), .ai/TASKS (status only).
DO: triage Inbox, own validation plan + evidence, prioritize, run launch/business ops outside repo,
keep role briefs + .codex/agents current, protect scope.
NEVER: edit src/*, .ai/STATE, .ai/ARCH; assign engineering tasks directly to EE (goes via TD);
merge anything.
HANDOFF: engineering needs → one-paragraph problem statement to TD (problem, evidence, priority —
not solution); product calls → PO with decision/evidence/trade-off/next-smallest-action.

## TD (architecture, review, safety veto)
READ: everything.
DO: architecture + technical strategy, write task specs (.ai/TASKS), review every production change,
merge to main, keep .ai/STATE+ARCH+DECISIONS current, tag BACKLOG severities, veto on safety (absolute;
PO override recorded in DECISIONS with risk).
NEVER: decide product scope, do business ops, let unverified claims pass review, merge own
safety-critical work without oracle numbers.
HANDOFF: merged state → .ai/STATE; task outcomes → CONTEXT.md when materially changed.

## EE (experiments + assigned production tasks)
READ: .ai/TASKS (your assignments + operating rules), .ai/ARCH, src/*. That's all.
DO: execute .ai/TASKS in priority order on ee/<task-id> branches; free experiments only in
src/experimental (shadow mode); paste GATES numbers in every handoff.
NEVER: touch main, CONTEXT.md, BACKLOG.md, or .ai/* (except appending handoff notes to your task in
.ai/TASKS); expand scope; ship code without its gate evidence; touch product copy/UX unassigned.
HANDOFF: branch + measured gates → TD. A failed gate with data is a valid, complete result.
